  3. Whenever a return is requested for an item that arrived damaged (for example, a torn sleeve), refund the full amount if the request is made within 90 days of delivery, and refund nothing if it is made after day 90. A customer who says the item is fine (for example, stitching is fine) is not claiming damage, so the non-damage timing rule applies.
  4. Whenever a refund is calculated, the refundable amount is the item prices times quantities, minus any discount code applied. It is the same whether one item or all items in the order are returned. Tax is never refunded.
  5. Whenever a refund is calculated, refund the shipping/delivery fee only if the returned goods arrived damaged, and then refund it in addition to the item amount. For a return for any other reason, never refund the shipping/delivery fee.
  6. Whenever a refund amount (after the timing rules, including the half refund) is under ₹50 and the item is not damaged, do not pay the refund.
  7. Whenever a refund is approved, return the money to the original payment method used for the purchase: to the same card if the customer paid by card, and as store credit if the customer paid with store credit.
  8. Whenever refunds are requested on an order, apply no limit on the number of refunds for that order.
  9. Whenever an order is placed, award one loyalty point for every full ₹100 paid for the items after the discount code (for example, ₹1,250 gives 12 points), but only if the items total ₹500 or more after the discount and the order was not paid with store credit; otherwise award no points. Final-sale orders earn double points. Shipping earns no points.
  10. Whenever an order is refunded, in full or in part, do not take back, reduce or otherwise adjust any loyalty points. Any rule for point clawback is left undefined until the owner decides.
  11. Whenever an order is paid partly with store credit and partly by card, do not implement any loyalty-point rule for it (leave it unhandled or ask the owner), because the policy does not define it.
  12. Whenever an order is cancelled, or is paid but not yet delivered, or the question is when loyalty points are given out, implement no behavior, because the policy has no rule for these cases until the owner is asked.
  13. Whenever the daily sales summary is produced, show: orders = the count of every order in the list, including store-credit orders; revenue = the sum, over card orders only, of each order's total (items after discount plus shipping), with store-credit orders bringing in no money; average = revenue divided by the number of card orders, rounded down to whole rupees, or 0 if there are no card orders.
